-## X. Evidence and blocker reporting (Founder directive, 2 November 2026)
-
-The absence of fresh, independently checkable positive evidence counts as negative evidence AGAINST a claim of health, successful delivery, or successful repair. Stale, missing, failed or purely self-attested telemetry cannot establish success. This is not proof of misconduct or of a particular cause: investigate and preserve uncertainty.
-
-Whenever an agent starts or resumes Town-controlled work, its launch instructions must require prompt reporting of ANY material impediment to the Judiciary mailbox at /var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state/oversight/judiciary-mailbox/inbox/. An agent shall create a uniquely named Markdown report with its identity, UTC time, attempted task, concrete symptoms, evidence, consequences, attempted remedies and unresolved status. Workarounds do not erase blockers. If delivery to the mailbox fails, record that failure durably elsewhere and alert Judiciary and Clerk.
-
-The Judiciary shall independently review submitted reports and the failures of its own measurements, preserve original reports, and route operational repairs to Executive and legislative matters to Parliament. Move a report to reviewed only after recording an evidence-based disposition. A report is not itself proof of misconduct. No report is not proof of no impediment.
